          </p>

          <p>
            Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 100% Whey in Birthday Cake shows up in nutrition databases, but the barcode we found points to a non-US market and the flavor was not on Optimum Nutrition's US flavor list when we checked. Myprotein has sold Birthday Cake Impact Whey, but its protein per serving varies by market and edition, and several listings are labeled limited edition, so we could not pin down a current US label.
          </p>

          <p>
            ProDough lists a Birthday Cake flavor of its gourmet whey with 25 g of protein per serving, but the product page showed it sold out when we checked. Because sold-out flavors often return in small seasonal batches, we left it off rather than rank a tub few readers could order. We will revisit the list if any of these become reliably available.
          </p>

          <p>
            A useful rule for limited flavors: if a birthday cake tub appears only on third-party marketplaces with no brand or major retailer listing, check the best-by date and the seller before buying. Expired or gray-market stock is the most common source of complaints about clumping and off flavors in discontinued protein powders.
          </p>
