                  Loosely, birthday cake flavors lean toward frosting and sprinkles, while cake batter leans toward buttery raw batter. In practice the protein base matters more: casein blends like PEScience taste thicker and more batter-like, while isolates taste lighter. Read the protein source and sweetener lines rather than relying on the flavor name to predict taste.
                </p>
